# Where a letter's name is asked for, and where Catalan answers first.
#
# char_name is the whole of the path a lone letter takes: single_chars walks
# the characters of a token it has decided to spell out and calls this for
# each of them, and this looks the character up in span_char_name, the
# language's dictionary of character names. That dictionary is Castilian's --
# it is the one of the six that was kept, because a letter with no name has
# nothing to say and crashes the rule that would have said it -- so x said
# ekis and h ache.
#
# A Catalan name cannot be put in the dictionary. The digits found out why
# and rules/constants records it: what tools/delta-dict.py writes is named by
# an address the arena does not know, so a record it rewrites comes out
# silent however carefully its length is kept. The way past it is the way the
# digits took, which is to say the word from a rule out of bytes of ours.
#
# So the rule is IBM's with one call in front of the dictionary's. Everything
# it does is done in the order it did it -- the same wrappers, the same test
# of the two state fields, the same choice point in front of span_char_name
# -- and cat_char_name is asked first. A letter it names is named and the
# dictionary is never reached; a character it says nothing about, which is
# twenty of the letters and every mark, digit and accented vowel, goes to the
# dictionary exactly as before.
#
# The test the rule opens with is IBM's and is kept rather than understood:
# two state fields held against each other, and the rule says nothing when
# they differ. Putting our arm behind it rather than in front means a
# character we would name is only named where Castilian would have named one.
#
# One letter is refused a name on purpose. Castilian's dictionary has no
# entry for a or o, because those are words in Spanish, and a token of one
# of them goes on to the lookup sets and is found there as a function word.
# It has an entry for i, and so the Catalan conjunction -- pa, vi i formatge
# -- was being named as a letter, which is a content word, and stressed in
# every sentence it stood in. The rule now says nothing for a lone i, and
# the token takes the path a and o take: coord_conjs holds it, and it is not
# stressed. The letter's name is the same sound, so a spelled-out i is not
# changed by this, only its stress when it stands alone.
rule char_name takes 3 from u_integ.obj
  local left bytes 8
  local right bytes 8
  call ZZget_parm_ptr2 addr left arg 1 addr right arg 2
  call ZZfence_null
  call ZZstarttest1
  raw load movw statefld 3230 into r0w
  if answer is not global half 3222
    call succeed
    answer 0
  end
  call ZZlpta_load__setscan_r__1 addr left             # a lone i is the
  if answer is 0                                       # conjunction, not a
    call ZZtest_string_s_1_1_ZZstring109               # letter to be named
    if answer is 0
      give up
    end
  end
  call cat_char_name addr left addr right              # Catalan's own six
  if answer is 0
    call succeed
    answer 0
  end
  call ZZstarttest2
  call ZZbspush_ca_boa__3
  call span_char_name addr left addr right
  if answer is not 0
    give up
  end
  call succeed
  answer 0
end
